WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.534 --> 00:00:18.198
When Zann and his friends burst out of the Hollow, Jev was trying to fend off the buzzing spy fly.

2
00:00:18.199 --> 00:00:22.589
"Wait, you crazy thing!" Jev complained as it flew at his head.

3
00:00:22.590 --> 00:00:26.170
"It's back!" Perda exclaimed. "What did it see?"

4
00:00:26.171 --> 00:00:30.427
Jev flapped his hand at the fly. "I don't know yet," he said.

5
00:00:30.428 --> 00:00:35.305
"I hate spy flies—I didn't want it in my ear more than once."

6
00:00:35.306 --> 00:00:41.837
"Well, we're here now," Zann said, trying to hide his impatience. "Let's hear what it saw."

7
00:00:41.838 --> 00:00:49.367
"Fine." Jev lowered his hand. The spy fly buzzed into his ear, burrowing deep inside. Jev grimaced.

8
00:00:49.368 --> 00:00:52.326
"What's it showing you?" Gliss asked.

9
00:00:52.327 --> 00:00:55.415
Zann held his breath as he waited for the answer.

10
00:00:55.416 --> 00:00:59.353
He'd used spy flies enough to know exactly what was happening.

11
00:00:59.354 --> 00:01:02.541
The little creature had found Morb, as Jev had ordered.

12
00:01:02.542 --> 00:01:07.095
And it had recorded everything it saw and heard in its tiny brain.

13
00:01:07.096 --> 00:01:11.600
Now it was back, ready to pour that information into Jev's mind.

14
00:01:11.601 --> 00:01:17.546
Jev closed his eyes. "It's flying toward some huge stone castle," he reported.

15
00:01:17.547 --> 00:01:20.934
"Is it the palace in First City?" Gliss asked.

16
00:01:20.935 --> 00:01:25.007
"No. It's on a mountain with forest all around.

17
00:01:25.008 --> 00:01:31.297
The fly is looking in some windows." Jev gasped. "Whoa! There are trolls in there!"

18
00:01:31.298 --> 00:01:34.728
"Trolls?" Zann exchanged a look with his friends.

19
00:01:34.729 --> 00:01:38.260
It sounded as if the spy fly had found the right place!

20
00:01:38.261 --> 00:01:41.926
"Okay, now it's looking in the window at a dungeon.

21
00:01:41.927 --> 00:01:47.205
There are people in cells, and—hey! There's your grandfather, Zann!"

22
00:01:47.206 --> 00:01:50.608
"Boz?" Zann exclaimed. "Is he okay?"

23
00:01:50.609 --> 00:01:53.176
"Are my parents there?" Gliss cried.

24
00:01:53.177 --> 00:01:55.417
"I don't know; I can't see them.

25
00:01:55.418 --> 00:01:58.152
But there are lots of people in the other cells.

26
00:01:58.153 --> 00:02:00.603
I think they're all Reds," Jev said.

27
00:02:00.604 --> 00:02:05.316
"Gross! The trolls are pulling leeches off Boz!"

28
00:02:05.317 --> 00:02:11.383
"Leeches?" Zann echoed, picturing the tiny, harmless creatures from the local swamp.

29
00:02:11.384 --> 00:02:14.233
Jev nodded. "I guess that's what they are.

30
00:02:14.234 --> 00:02:16.420
I've never seen leeches like these, though.

31
00:02:16.421 --> 00:02:22.280
They're huge—and blue! Boz is yelling at some tall, skinny guy who's watching.

32
00:02:22.281 --> 00:02:26.803
Is that Morb? Oh wait—now the fly is going to a different window.

33
00:02:26.804 --> 00:02:33.208
The tall guy just came in. More trolls too. They're carrying a big black pot . . ."

34
00:02:33.209 --> 00:02:38.661
He went on, describing everything the spy fly had seen: Morb lighting the fire.

35
00:02:38.662 --> 00:02:45.812
The leeches burning to a crisp. Morb breathing in the blue steam. His triumphant laugh.

36
00:02:45.813 --> 00:02:49.982
"Now Morb is leaving," Jev said. "No, wait—he just turned around.

37
00:02:49.983 --> 00:02:56.203
Wow! He totally blasted that black pot to smithereens, just by pointing at it!

38
00:02:56.204 --> 00:03:00.909
I didn't even see him make any friction before he did it!" Jev's eyes flew open.

39
00:03:00.910 --> 00:03:05.421
His usual cocky expression was gone, replaced by nervousness.

40
00:03:05.422 --> 00:03:08.550
"That's it," he said quickly. "There's no more."

41
00:03:08.551 --> 00:03:11.213
"Are you sure?" Perda asked.

42
00:03:11.214 --> 00:03:13.952
Jev shook the spy fly out of his ear.

43
00:03:13.953 --> 00:03:17.347
The creature buzzed around in a circle, and then flew off.

44
00:03:17.348 --> 00:03:20.956
"I'm sure," Jev said, his voice shaking.

45
00:03:20.957 --> 00:03:25.868
"And look, if you want any more favors, find someone else, okay? I'm done with this."

46
00:03:25.869 --> 00:03:29.118
"What?" Perda exclaimed. "But Jev . . ."

47
00:03:29.119 --> 00:03:32.700
"I told you we couldn't trust him," Zann put in.

48
00:03:32.701 --> 00:03:36.165
Jev shot him a glare. "Don't worry; I'll keep your secrets.

49
00:03:36.166 --> 00:03:40.514
But that's it. I'm not risking my own neck for a couple of Reds."

50
00:03:40.515 --> 00:03:43.744
Gliss looked hurt. "I thought we were friends!"

51
00:03:43.745 --> 00:03:48.715
Jev shrugged. "See you guys later," he muttered without meeting anyone's eye.

52
00:03:48.716 --> 00:03:54.106
He took off without another word, running a few steps and then zapping himself out of sight.

53
00:03:54.107 --> 00:03:56.645
"What a jerk," Zann muttered.

54
00:03:56.646 --> 00:04:00.469
"Forget him," Perda said. "Let's figure out what this means.

55
00:04:00.470 --> 00:04:02.965
Where do you think that castle could be?"

56
00:04:02.966 --> 00:04:05.858
"Mount Mystery," Darb said immediately.

57
00:04:05.859 --> 00:04:08.734
"There's an ancient stone fortress up there."

58
00:04:08.735 --> 00:04:13.651
The others stared at him in surprise. "How do you know that?" Zann asked.

59
00:04:13.652 --> 00:04:16.291
"I read a lot." Darb looked thoughtful.

60
00:04:16.292 --> 00:04:22.393
"Morb must have found some bigger leeches and figured out how to make his old method of stealing magic work better.

61
00:04:22.394 --> 00:04:25.921
First the leeches suck the magic out of his prisoners.

62
00:04:25.922 --> 00:04:30.771
Then he cooks the leeches and breathes in the magic when it comes out as steam."

63
00:04:30.772 --> 00:04:33.822
Gliss shuddered. "That's horrible!"

64
00:04:33.823 --> 00:04:38.126
"But where would he find big blue leeches?" Perda said.

65
00:04:38.127 --> 00:04:44.746
Zann and Darb traded a look. "Probably the same place he got those stinging dragons," Darb said.

66
00:04:44.747 --> 00:04:46.919
"Huh?" Perda said.

67
00:04:46.920 --> 00:04:51.683
"I bet Morb got those leeches from a different world!" Zann said.

68
00:04:51.684 --> 00:04:55.137
"You mean like the ones your parents visited?" Perda asked.

69
00:04:55.138 --> 00:05:01.682
"Exactly. If Morb worked at their lab, he might have figured out how to access a wormhole."

70
00:05:01.683 --> 00:05:04.709
"But how could he—" Gliss began.

71
00:05:04.710 --> 00:05:09.031
"I don't know," Zann cut her off. "I don't have all the answers yet.

72
00:05:09.032 --> 00:05:13.517
But I know one thing. We've got to warn people about this."

73
00:05:13.518 --> 00:05:17.540
Darb nodded. "Let's go find the mayor and show her the diary.

74
00:05:17.541 --> 00:05:19.994
She'll know how to get word to the palace."

75
00:05:19.995 --> 00:05:24.264
"Good idea," Perda agreed.

76
00:05:24.265 --> 00:05:29.510
But when they arrived at the town hall, Zann and his friends got a nasty surprise.

77
00:05:29.511 --> 00:05:36.824
The mayor was gone! People were frantically running around and shouting, and nobody paid any attention to the kids.

78
00:05:36.825 --> 00:05:42.957
"I guess Morb broke through the mayor's Shield spell," Perda said as they watched from behind some shrubs.

79
00:05:42.958 --> 00:05:46.040
"Now what?" Gliss' voice shook a little.

80
00:05:46.041 --> 00:05:50.721
Zann took a deep breath. "We have no choice.

81
00:05:50.722 --> 00:05:55.214
Tomorrow we'll have to bring Boz's diary to the palace ourselves.

82
00:05:55.215 --> 00:05:59.436
We can also tell the king and queen what we learned from the spy fly."

83
00:05:59.437 --> 00:06:04.712
"But how are we supposed to get all the way to First City on our own?" Perda asked.

84
00:06:04.713 --> 00:06:10.090
Zann noticed that Darb was looking thoughtful again. "What?" Zann asked him.

85
00:06:10.091 --> 00:06:16.848
Darb smiled. "I have an idea."
